=========================================================================
RECOMMENDATIONS FOR NEXT PHASE
=========================================================================

1. RESOLUTION INCREASE: Try 448px with this bbox model. The bbox crop already focuses
   on the bird, so higher resolution would add more detail to the bird region specifically.
   Batch size would need to drop to 8-10 at 448px.

2. TEST-TIME AUGMENTATION (TTA): The model fluctuates +/-0.25pp between epochs.
   TTA (multi-crop, flip averaging) could stabilize predictions and add 0.3-0.5pp.

3. STOCHASTIC WEIGHT AVERAGING (SWA): Average weights from epochs 29-35 (all within
   0.38pp of best). This could smooth the accuracy fluctuations.

4. ENSEMBLE WITH NON-BBOX MODEL: The bbox model (92.25%) and non-bbox model (91.75%)
   likely make different errors. Ensembling could push to 93%+.

5. FURTHER LR REDUCTION: A third phase with LR=2e-6 (the sweet spot from this run)
   starting from epoch 30 checkpoint could squeeze out another 0.1-0.3pp.

6. NO REGULARIZATION CHANGES NEEDED: The train-val gap is small and stable.
   MixUp is working well. No need to increase or decrease regularization.

